\openmidiport opens a MIDI output port.
It takes one argument, the number of the port, as printed
by \listmidiports:

\listmidiports
\openmidiport 1

\listmidiports must be called first, otherwise you will
get a "MIDI port doesn't exist" error, as the list of
ports is read by that command.
A port can be opened only once. Opening it again gives
an error.

Once open, the port can be used by \ctlchange and
\pgmchange. Instruments open their port with their
midiport method, so you don't need this command for them:

\inst1.midiport 1
